From f1d0666b9fc80d25a7c4cbacf4025f3a33152111 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:01:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] Linux hold: bind lease permits to their decision;
 confirmed-stop teardown on every path

Root review (ROOT-LINUX-DECISION-WINDOW-REVIEW.txt), verified through the actual tryClaim/renewLeases flows (the b744ba19
control dispatches a claim and a renewal; with the real lease client the claim reaches the relay):

1. Permit capture. walletSendGate read the refused/unknown counter when the GATE was built (after await openForUs), so an
   allow decided before a later refusal was rebased onto the newer count and accepted.
   - The permit now belongs to the decision: the record snapshot (leasePermit: object, epoch, status) is taken by the
     caller before its first await (renewLeases before the ledger read, auditClaims before the decision), the
     per-deployment counter when the decision STARTS. The gate compares against those, never re-captures.
   - An allow whose read overlapped a refused/unknown answer (an old in-flight read returning after a newer withdrawal)
     is read again; a second overlap answers unknown. A decision started after a withdrawal is a fresh allow and stands.

2. Teardown paths. tearDown(rec, status, why): withdrawService (status, streams, egress, permits) and a pending-stop mark
   BEFORE the stop's await, then the slice freed only on a confirmed stop (settleStop). Used by the reaper (lease over,
   out of funded time), owner setActive(false), a lost lease, the share-resize eviction, abandonClaims, the ledger move,
   the publisher yank, the admin consolidation release, the owner DELETE route, and the wallet hold/refusal paths. Each
   path's LEASE rule (release / keep / lapse) is unchanged. The owner move route keeps its rule (release only on a
   confirmed DELETE) and frees its slice via settleStop; the envelope-edit relaunch now defers on an unconfirmed stop
   (the version switch's existing rule). The DELETE route reports instanceStopConfirmed instead of implying it.
   - reconcilePools dropped every terminal record's handle within 60 s, freeing a pending-stop slice while the guest may
     still run: a terminal record with _stopPending now keeps its hold (restore already re-reserves it).

Tests: decision-window cases through the real tryClaim/renewLeases (both senders), the converted teardown paths on a
failed and a confirmed stop, restart/accounting (real loadState, reconcilePools, releaseGpu), a POOL_SELFTEST process
case, and test/supervisor-wallet-real-lease-client.test.mjs: the supervisor's tryClaim -> sendLeaseTx driving the REAL
lease client and relay service on anvil. Shared vm fixture moved to test/helpers/supervisor-wallet-fixture.mjs.
